Modifications made in this fork (github.com/kelnei/rewrite-body), relative to
upstream v1.2.0 (commit a37d560, 24 November 2022):

  * go.mod, all Go import paths, and .traefik.yml were updated from
    github.com/packruler/rewrite-body to github.com/kelnei/rewrite-body so the
    module path matches this repository.

  * logger/logger.go: the Log*f methods now check the configured log level
    before formatting the message. Previously fmt.Sprintf was passed as an
    argument to writeLog and therefore evaluated unconditionally, so discarded
    log lines still built their message in full. Because the handler logs the
    whole response body twice per request, this allocated roughly twice the
    page size on every request even with logging disabled.

  * logger/logger_format_test.go was added to cover the above.
